00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:40,760
 the real winners will be the ones that take bits from all the different industries.

189
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:52,620
 So, there's so much random stuff being done, and I think leadership are not putting guidelines

190
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:53,620
 in place.

191
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:57,620
 So, you know, from our side, it's actually less experimentation.

192
00:12:57,620 --> 00:13:01,480
 You only can do it if there's a productivity gain.

193
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:06,720
 You know, don't waste your time, I'm not saying, you know, don't try it, but don't waste your

194
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:11,080
 time on tons of experiments when your customer wants your value.

195
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:15,120
 You know, at the end of the day, it's the customer that's paying for you.

196
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:17,260
 So, you know, what is driving value?

197
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:24,740
 So, in our business, we're really, really strict in terms of what our vectors are, and unless

198
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:31,080
 it's adding a productivity gain, you don't do it, unless it's approved for some other reason.

199
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:37,640
 And I think, how do you tie that productivity gain is have a really clear vision.

200
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:41,180
 You know, a brilliant book by Cameron Herald called Vivid Vision.

201
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:47,520
 You should all write that down and read it, but, you know, don't have a one-paragraph vision

202
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:48,520
 statement.

203
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:54,940
 Write a 20-page document of how you see the business, or get whoever the CEO or your manager,

